WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:01.134 line:92%
-Our first guests tonight

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
are 13-time
Grammy Award-winning musicians

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the highest-selling
U.S. female band in history.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
Their latest album,
"Gaslighter," is available now

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.777 line:92%
Please welcome to the show

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:13.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
the legendary Natalie Maines
Emily Strayer,

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Martie Maguire
of The Chicks.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi.
-How are you?

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks for having us.
-It is lovely

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have you all here,
albeit virtually.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:26.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know that two of you
are in Texas.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.394 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Natalie, you're in L.A.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:31.564
How are you --
How have you handled quarantine?

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:34.034 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-[ Laughs ] Splendidly.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.902 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's amazing.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:36.503 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yes, I would say

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm definitely the most
sequestered of the three of us

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.143 line:92%
But I did had to go to the DMV

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:47.113 size:88% position:44%
which is a scary place
even without quarantine.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:52.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
But my son turned 16
and wanted his driving test.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.621 size:78% position:39% line:92%
So I did battle that.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:57.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
The scariest part of that
was the porta-potty.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:58.725 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yeah, well, they say

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:02.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
try to avoid the porta-potties
at the DMV at all costs.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But this is --

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.132
I think, is it Martie,
you also have 16-year-old twins.

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:09.102 size:84% position:42%
Are they going through
their driving, as well?

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.837 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Um, they're about to.

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-Yeah, they have permits,

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:15.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, yeah,
they just turned 16 in April

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two at the same time.
I'm terrified.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.146 line:92%
-Because of social distancing,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:23.783
can you have sort of driving
instructors in a car with you?

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:24.818 size:84% position:42% line:92%
How does that work now?

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:27.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, and I have been out
a couple times

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.655 line:92%
with one of them in particular

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:32.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughing ] And it's
white-knuckling, you know.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, I have my boyfrien
take them out,

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he's a lot
braver than I am.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I guess
if you don't have a special ca

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:43.002
where you have that driver's e
brake on the passenger side,

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
it can be a terrifying
experience.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, quite.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, Emily,
congratulations are in order

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:51.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it your oldest
that's getting into college,

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.312 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
got into college?

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. I got my first kid
off to college.

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we didn't have to set foot
on a campus.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just did a drive-by,
just waved

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then looked at
all the majors that they had

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:05.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was a good fit.
And he applied and got in.

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.060 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And, so, I'm happy.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's --
Congratulations to him.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:11.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he never walked around
the campus earlier in his life

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.032 line:92%
It was just, it looked good,

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you drove by,
and that was enough?

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's familiar
with that part of the country.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:19.739
So I knew he knew the area
the people, and everything

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was just, we were just
looking for majors

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:22.609 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
more than anything.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:26.479 size:84% position:42%
But, yeah, we didn't do
any, you know, visits

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:27.213 size:81% position:41% line:92%
or anything like that.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's probably good for him,
too, though.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:30.817 line:92%
-Well, that will make his --

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whenever he finally
gets on campus,

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
it will be
a whole new experience.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:36.556 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:39.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
Guys, congratulations
on the album.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:41.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's fantastic
all the way through.

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:43.229 line:92%
The title track is fantastic

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
But certainly,
the world we live in

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:48.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
interrupted the rollout
of this album,

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:49.536 size:88% position:44% line:92%
up to including the fact

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:52.739
that we were going to all
get together in the spring

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:54.073 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and day-drink together.

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was looking forward to i
a great deal.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.511
Do you think you would hav
drank me under the table?

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that --
Were you confident of that

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What's --
What's your drink of ch--

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
What would you
have been drinking?

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I grabbed a tequila
right now, so --

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's what we drink.
-What do you guys have?

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you have something?
-Tequila.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Tequila.
-Wine.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. Great. [ Laughs ]
-Red wine.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.661 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I'm sorry, rosé wine.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would say --
-Oh, well, I feel like

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.932 size:81% position:41%
Martie would have been
under the table, then.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:19.899 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right, Martie's --

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:22.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We could drink you
under the table, I think.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:25.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My tolerance has gone way u
during corona.

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think it broke
one way or the other, right?

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:31.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think people either
really built up their toleranc

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
or now people are
total lightweights.

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:34.247 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I'm scared, actually.

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:38.685
Every day, I ask my boyfriend,
"Do you think I'm an alcoholic

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:41.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think I'm an alcoholic?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.423 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-And what does he say?

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:45.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Excellent.
-I think historically,

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
the people
who have to ask every day

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:51.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
are usually
on the wrong side of it.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.265 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:55.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Right. If I'm willin
to ask, I'm probably not.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But Martie weighs
like 8 pounds,

00:03:56.703 --> 00:04:01.174
so like two glasses of wine, and
she's just like really tipsy

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.141 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:04.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What -- You know,
a lot of people, I think,

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially in the very
beginning of this,

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.114 line:92%
wondered if this would be a time

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:12.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
that would increase or decreas
their creativity.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.320 line:92%
How did you find it as --

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.689
Was this a time that you sort of
thrived creatively,

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:20.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
or did you find yourself
being blocked?

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.629 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh, not musically.

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:25.398 line:92%
Have not created a single note

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:30.403
But I always have craft projects
and house projects,

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.705
and around the holidays,
I've been making wreaths.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
Would you like to see them
-I would love to see a wreath.

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.043 size:81% position:41%
This is very exciting.
-I thought you might.

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:40.013 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So I have them on hand.

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:41.381 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Oh, that's very nice!

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:42.682 size:88% position:44% line:92%
That looks professional.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:47.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you. Etsy professional.
Here's one more.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.655 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's see.

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:51.324 line:92%
[ Grunts ] This one's big.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.158 size:75% position:38% line:92%
This one is for you.

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God!
That is absolutely --

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:56.162 line:92%
Now, how long, start to finish

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
does it take
to make a wreath that size

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.067 line:92%
-This one, I made yesterday.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:04.671 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it took me...

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:06.706 line:92%
I'm going to say six hours

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's --
-Really? That's it?

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That seems about right.
-I binge-watched

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:15.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
