and made that wreath.

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:15.848 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:19.352
-I don't know what could b
more Christmassy than that

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:23.156
Martie and Emily, were you aware
that Natalie was making wreaths?

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:25.458 size:84% position:42%
Is this -- Are you guys
close enough as a band

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:27.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this information
made it to you?

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.395 line:92%
-I didn't know specifically,

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I did not --
It was not a shock to me.

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:34.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's always doing
something, like, crafty.

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.402 line:92%
One year, it was latch hooks

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:39.072
She was going to make --
-[ Laughing ] That's right

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:39.872 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-And then, you know --

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:43.042 size:75% position:38%
-I did the entire --
What's the supper,

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.644 line:92%
the supper from the Bible?

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:46.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"The Last Supper"?
-"The Last Supper."

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:49.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
I latch-hooked
"The Last Supper."

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:51.351 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:52.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Where is that?
Do you have that handy?

00:05:52.819 --> 00:05:55.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I should stress to you guys
I'm not religious,

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:57.423 line:92%
and I got that right away.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.525 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:02.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which supper?
-I'm not real religious.

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:04.097 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:05.631 line:92%
-"Oh, she -- She did a painting.

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.200 line:92%
You remember The Big Supper?

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't think
it's called that."

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:10.203 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.738 line:92%
-Wait, was it the first supper

00:06:11.738 --> 00:06:13.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
or the second
to the last supper?

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:18.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Stick to wreaths.
-[ Laughing ] The last supper.

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:21.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, this is --
You know, this is a very -

00:06:21.748 --> 00:06:22.982 line:92%
It seems to me that your fans,

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:25.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
and correct me if I'm wrong,
they --

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:26.419 line:92%
When you guys release work

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:29.422
because you have fans that car
a great deal about your work

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:32.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
they try to delve
into the lyrics especially

00:06:32.225 --> 00:06:33.926 line:92%
and try to find meaning in them,

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:37.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
a brand of, I guess,
fan sleuthing.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:39.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that fun for you guys
when people do that,

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:42.869 line:92%
and how close do they get?

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:44.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't watch
a whole lot of it,

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:49.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
but some of it's close.
Some of it's not.

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:51.511 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:54.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, you know, we didn't
want to spell it all out.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.749 line:92%
We wanted people to get to

00:06:56.749 --> 00:06:59.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of decipher the album
for themselves.

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:03.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
And some of their guesses
that I've seen have been right

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:04.991 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and some have not.

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:08.060 line:92%
I will say, I do not own a boat.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:12.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that seems to be
everyone's biggest question.

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:13.733 line:92%
-Well, you should make one

00:07:13.733 --> 00:07:17.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
You obviously are very crafty.
-Mm-hmm.

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:19.372 line:92%
-You must all be excited.

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:21.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
there's a million reasons

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:22.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be excited
for this to be over.

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:24.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I imagine,
like, these are songs

00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:28.381
that you haven't had much of
a chance to play live together

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:30.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not at all.
-Yeah.

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:31.017 line:92%
-We were supposed to go --

00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:32.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were supposed
to release the album in May,

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:35.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
go on tour in June.
None of that happened.

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:37.723
We had to kind of fight with
the label to get the album out

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:39.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause we just wanted everybod
to have the music.

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:43.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
But probably won't tour
for another year and a half.

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:44.630 line:92%
-Well, when the time comes

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:48.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we can all be
in places and rooms together

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:52.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope we can get our
day-drinking back on the books

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:53.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a delight
to talk to you all.

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:55.274 line:92%
Thanks so much for being here.

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:57.543 line:92%
-Thanks so much for having us.

